        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.086,
            0.548,
            0.111
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "8.2 Another Mystery"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.115,
            0.886,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "Next day, Aavi, Thirav and their friends decide to make lemonade. During the preparation, they take cold water in a glass tumbler and add ice cubes into it. After a few minutes, they notice something exciting about the outer surface of the glass tumbler."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.284,
            0.217,
            0.883,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "Let us find out by conducting a similar activity ourselves."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.25,
            0.591,
            0.272
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 8.3: Let us experiment"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.282,
            0.668,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": " Take cold water in a glass tumbler."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.308,
            0.794,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": " Add a few ice cubes into it as shown in Fig. 8.2."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.338,
            0.346,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.139,
                0.458,
                0.427,
                0.492
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.2: A glass tumbler containing cold water and ice cubes"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.335,
            0.807,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": " Leave it undisturbed for five minutes and observe it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.382,
            0.884,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": " **Record** your observations and the questions that arise in your mind in Table 8.1. You can also touch the outer surface of the glass tumbler to feel if there is any change."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.504,
            0.83,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": "You may have many observations and questions here."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.261,
            0.564,
            0.876,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "| I observe | I wonder |\n| --- | --- |\n|  |  |\n|  |  |\n|  |  |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.304,
                0.535,
                0.803,
                0.556
              ],
              "content": "Table 8.1: Record the observations and questions"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_table_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.714,
            0.885,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": "One observation that arises in Aavi’s mind is, “There are some water droplets (tiny drops) appearing on the outer surface of the glass tumbler.” Initially, water droplets are deposited and these droplets combine together to form bigger drops. You can also try the above process with a metal container. You may be curious about where the water droplets come from."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.857,
            0.885,
            0.9
          ],
          "content": "Suggest possible reasons explaining the appearance of water droplets on the outer surface of the glass tumbler."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
